 # Settler landing: complete the handoff to the land party
 
+## Correction: why the ship still waited offshore
+
+The fix described below did not make settlers land. In the game the galley
+sailed to the water tile next to the chosen site and stayed there, settler and
+escort aboard. Running the real DLL headlessly (a harness that loads this DLL,
+the mod's XML and a scripted two-island map, and lets the AI play) shows why.
+Each turn after the first leg the ship logged `MISSING_ESCORT_OR_CAPACITY` and
+skipped.
+
+`AI_settlerSeaTransport` recognised the escort with `canDefend()`. Without a
+plot argument, `CvUnit::canDefend` asks about the unit's own plot, and a land
+unit aboard a ship at sea is on water. `isValidDomainForAction` fails there,
+and `LAND_UNITS_CAN_ATTACK_WATER_CITIES` is 0, so the answer is false. In port
+the escort counted and the ship sailed. At sea, including on the tile in front
+of the site, the ship had no escort, and the landing code below never ran. The
+tests passed because their stand-in `canDefend()` ignored the plot.
+
+A second engine detail broke the hand-off once landing worked. `CvUnit::setXY`
+moves every unit that leaves a transport into a new group of its own. The
+settler and escort reached land as two groups without `MISSIONAI_FOUND`, which
+contradicts what the tests asserted.
+
+Changes:
+
+- Escorts aboard are recognised with `canFight()`, which is what `canDefend()`
+  checks apart from the plot.
+- After a delivered landing, the escort rejoins the settler's group and the
+  group gets `MISSIONAI_FOUND` and the site again. `AI_settleMove` founds there
+  next turn (landing from water uses all of a unit's moves).
+- `Tools/test_settler_landing.py` now models both engine rules. Against the
+  previous source 9 of its 14 cases fail; with only the escort change, the 2
+  cases that check the destination survives landing still fail; with both
+  changes all 14 pass.
+
+Real DLL, 30 AI turns, settler, warrior escort and galley on a one-city island:
+
+| Build | Site 6 tiles away | Site 10 tiles away |
+|---|---|---|
+| Before | galley waits next to the site for 29 turns, no city | waits 28 turns, no city |
+| After | lands turn 2, founds turn 3 | lands turn 3, founds turn 4 |
+
+The rest of this document describes the earlier change, which remains in
+place.
+
 This fix targets GitLab **`b8c379c1ffad9cd5408ca0e43dca88daf8ba85ee`**, including the user's imports of settlement placement and joint settlement planning. It changes only `CvUnitAI::AI_settlerSeaTransport` at runtime. Apply [patch 0008](https://github.com/GertaBool/RoM/blob/main/fixes/0008-settler-landing.patch) with its [manifest](https://github.com/GertaBool/RoM/blob/main/fixes/landing-manifest.json); do not reapply 0007 to this base.
 
 ## What the investigation establishes
